1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,220
Social Studies, Class 5.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Lesson 2: Earth Movement.

3
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:06,760
Learning Objectives.

4
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:09,000
By the end of this chapter,

5
00:00:09,620 --> 00:00:11,060
learners will be able to:

6
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:13,900
Understand that the Earth is spherical.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,380
Identify the two types of movements of

8
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:17,900
the Earth.

9
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:20,920
Explain rotation and its effects.

10
00:00:21,740 --> 00:00:24,320
Understand revolution and its effects.

11
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:28,040
Learn about different seasons caused by revolution.

12
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:32,080
Define solstices and equinoxes and when they

13
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:32,480
occur.

14
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:34,380
Start-Up Activity.

15
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:37,340
Take a ball and spin it.

16
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:39,260
Notice how it moves.

17
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:42,960
Imagine this is the Earth moving in

18
00:00:43,040 --> 00:00:43,360
space.

19
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:47,880
The Earth moves in two ways—let's explore

20
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:49,720
these movements and their effects!

21
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:52,420
Who proved that the earth is spherical?

22
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:56,840
Many ancient civilizations believed that the Earth

23
00:00:56,920 --> 00:00:57,500
was flat.

24
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:01,980
However, Greek philosopher Pythagoras was one of

25
00:01:02,060 --> 00:01:04,000
the first to suggest that the Earth

26
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:04,720
is spherical.

27
00:01:05,520 --> 00:01:09,380
Later, Aristotle provided evidence by observing how

28
00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:12,300
ships disappear over the horizon and how

29
00:01:12,380 --> 00:01:14,320
the Earth's shadow on the Moon is

30
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:16,160
curved during a lunar eclipse.

31
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:20,024
Ferdinand Magellan's voyage around the world further

32
00:01:20,104 --> 00:01:21,940
confirmed that the Earth is round.

33
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:24,720
The Two Movements of the Earth.

34
00:01:25,740 --> 00:01:27,740
The Earth moves in two ways:

35
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:31,400
Rotation – The Earth spins on its

36
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:32,920
axis around itself.

37
00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:37,040
Revolution – The Earth moves around the

38
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:37,440
Sun.

39
00:01:38,320 --> 00:01:38,780
Rotation.

40
00:01:38,860 --> 00:01:41,880
The movement of the Earth around its

41
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:43,980
own axis is called rotation.

42
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:47,400
The earth rotates from west to east.

43
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:50,980
It completes one full rotation in 24

44
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:51,380
hours.

45
00:01:52,060 --> 00:01:54,360
The speed of rotation is faster at

46
00:01:54,440 --> 00:01:56,800
the equator and slower at the poles.

47
00:01:57,620 --> 00:01:59,800
The axis is tilted at an angle

48
00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:02,274
of 23.5°.

49
00:02:02,460 --> 00:02:04,560
As the Earth is spherical in shape,

50
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:07,080
only one half of the Earth receives

51
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:08,320
sunlight at a time.

52
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:10,980
Thus, the side of the Earth facing

53
00:02:11,060 --> 00:02:12,900
the Sun experience day.

54
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:14,420
On the other hand,

55
00:02:14,820 --> 00:02:15,640
the other half,

56
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:17,720
or the part away from the sun,

57
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:19,200
experiences night.

58
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:21,360
As the Earth rotates,

59
00:02:21,620 --> 00:02:24,080
the lighted part moves into the darkness.

60
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:28,125
This rotation causes day and night.

61
00:02:28,205 --> 00:02:28,840
Do You Know?

62
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:31,520
The Earth rotates at a speed of

63
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:35,960
1,670 kilometers per hour at the equator,

64
00:02:36,620 --> 00:02:38,585
but we don’t feel it because we’re

65
00:02:38,665 --> 00:02:39,840
moving along with it!

66
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:41,360
Revolution.

67
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:44,560
Revolution is the movement of the Earth

68
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:46,860
around the Sun in a fixed path

69
00:02:46,940 --> 00:02:48,060
called an orbit.

70
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:50,980
The Earth revolves around the Sun in

71
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:52,180
an elliptical orbit.

72
00:02:52,820 --> 00:02:55,140
It takes three hundred and sixty-five and

73
00:02:55,220 --> 00:02:58,180
one quarter days (one year) to complete

74
00:02:58,260 --> 00:02:59,180
one revolution.

75
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:02,240
The tilt of the Earth's axis remains

76
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:04,040
the same during revolution.

77
00:03:05,380 --> 00:03:07,060
Revolution causes seasonal changes.

78
00:03:07,780 --> 00:03:09,760
The revolution of the Earth and the

79
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:12,460
tilt of its axis cause different seasons:

80
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:16,220
Summer – The hemisphere tilted towards the

81
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:17,880
Sun experiences summer.

82
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:21,520
Winter – The hemisphere tilted away from

83
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:23,380
the Sun experiences winter.

84
00:03:24,260 --> 00:03:27,120
Spring – Occurs between winter and summer

85
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:29,160
when the temperature starts rising.

86
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:32,600
Autumn – Occurs between summer and winter

87
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:34,600
when the temperature starts dropping.

88
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:36,540
Let's Learn More.

89
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:39,880
A day on Earth is actually 23

90
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:41,620
hours, 56 minutes,

91
00:03:42,260 --> 00:03:44,120
not exactly 24 hours,

92
00:03:44,700 --> 00:03:46,460
but we round it off to 24

93
00:03:46,540 --> 00:03:48,760
hours because it’s easier to keep track

94
00:03:48,840 --> 00:03:49,220
of time.

95
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:52,300
What is Solstice and When Does It

96
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:52,700
Occur?

97
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:54,880
A solstice is a day,

98
00:03:54,960 --> 00:03:57,620
when the sun shines vertically over a

99
00:03:57,700 --> 00:04:01,060
Tropic (both cancer and Capricorn) in the

100
00:04:01,140 --> 00:04:03,540
afternoon and the day is the longest

101
00:04:03,620 --> 00:04:04,700
in that hemisphere.

102
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:07,280
On the twenty-second of December,

103
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:09,720
the rays of the sun fall directly

104
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:11,520
over the Tropic of Capricorn.

105
00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:14,340
This is the longest day in Southern

106
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:16,140
Hemisphere (summer season),

107
00:04:16,540 --> 00:04:17,980
while in the Northern Hemisphere,

108
00:04:18,380 --> 00:04:20,680
it is the shortest day (winter season).

109
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:23,380
This is called 'Winter Solstice.

110
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:25,760
On the twenty-first of June,

111
00:04:26,420 --> 00:04:28,800
sunlight falls vertically over the Tropic of

112
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:29,200
Cancer.

113
00:04:29,880 --> 00:04:32,020
This is the longest day in Northern

114
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:35,535
Hemisphere and hence it is called 'Summer

115
00:04:35,627 --> 00:04:37,640
Solstice', while in the Southern Hemisphere,

116
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:39,180
it is the shortest day.

117
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:40,960
Let's Learn More.

118
00:04:42,140 --> 00:04:44,320
Earth keeps rotating due to inertia,

119
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:47,620
the same reason you continue moving forward

120
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:49,560
when you stop a bike suddenly.

121
00:04:50,300 --> 00:04:53,080
This movement doesn’t stop because there’s no

122
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:55,100
friction in space to slow it down!

123
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,200
What is Equinox and When Does It

124
00:04:58,280 --> 00:04:58,600
Occur?

125
00:04:59,260 --> 00:05:01,640
The sun falls directly on the equator

126
00:05:01,720 --> 00:05:03,060
two times in a year.

127
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:06,240
During this period there is equal length

128
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:08,280
of day and night all over the

129
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:08,680
world.

130
00:05:09,220 --> 00:05:10,380
In Northern Hemisphere,

131
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:13,280
the March Equinox is called the Vernal

132
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:16,960
or Spring Equinox while September Equinox is

133
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:18,580
called Autumnal Equinox.

134
00:05:19,300 --> 00:05:23,200
Spring Equinox (March 21st) marks the beginning

135
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:23,940
of spring.

136
00:05:24,780 --> 00:05:28,560
Autumn Equinox (September 23rd) marks the beginning

137
00:05:28,640 --> 00:05:29,340
of autumn.

138
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:30,640
Recall.

139
00:05:31,380 --> 00:05:32,660
The Earth's movements,

140
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:34,860
rotation and revolution,

141
00:05:34,940 --> 00:05:37,720
have significant affects on our lives.

142
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:40,780
Rotation causes day and night,

143
00:05:41,260 --> 00:05:43,660
while revolution leads to the change of

144
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:44,080
seasons.

145
00:05:45,260 --> 00:05:48,160
Solstices and equinoxes mark the shift in

146
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:51,020
seasons, playing an essential role in our

147
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:52,440
climate and timekeeping.

148
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:54,360
Let's Remember.

149
00:05:54,980 --> 00:05:57,000
The Earth moves in two ways:

150
00:05:58,180 --> 00:05:59,320
rotation and revolution.

151
00:06:00,140 --> 00:06:02,220
Rotation causes day and night,

152
00:06:02,620 --> 00:06:04,620
while revolution causes seasons.

153
00:06:05,540 --> 00:06:08,460
The Earth completes one rotation in 24

154
00:06:08,540 --> 00:06:11,441
hours and one revolution in three hundred

155
00:06:11,521 --> 00:06:13,860
and sixty-five and one quarter days.

156
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:17,260
Solstices occur in June and December,

157
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:20,000
marking the longest and shortest days.

158
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:23,460
Equinoxes occur in March and September,

159
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:25,840
when day and night are equal.

160
00:06:26,640 --> 00:06:27,320
Word Bank.

161
00:06:28,180 --> 00:06:30,860
Rotation – Spinning of the Earth on

162
00:06:30,940 --> 00:06:31,580
its axis.

163
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:35,720
Revolution – Movement of the Earth around

164
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:36,220
the Sun.

165
00:06:37,180 --> 00:06:39,340
Orbit – The path of the Earth

166
00:06:39,420 --> 00:06:40,480
around the Sun.

167
00:06:41,420 --> 00:06:43,540
Solstice – When the Sun is at

168
00:06:43,620 --> 00:06:46,060
its farthest point north or south.

169
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:49,500
Equinox – When day and night are

170
00:06:49,580 --> 00:06:49,940
equal.
